    "report": "The contact details came back hidden because the paid-stay check ignored paid bookings that had since been cancelled. I fixed that and committed it on `main` as `74866d0`. Nothing was pushed.\n\n**Cause:** `hasPaidStay` in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts` had an extra condition, `b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Once the traveller cancelled, no paid booking matched, so `GetConversationQueryHandler` masked the host's contact details again. ADR 55 says a paid stay keeps lifting the hold \"whatever its status now\", so the condition contradicted the decision.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the status condition. The query still requires a payment with status `paid` or `declared` on a booking of the traveller for the listing. Nothing else about what the conversation shows changed.\n\n**Test:** I extended the existing \"Contact details held back\" e2e test in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. After the booking is paid, the traveller cancels it, and the host's phone-or-email message must still read in full with `masked: false`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `yarn test:e2e`: 114 suites, 607 tests, all passing. The path argument I passed was ignored, so this ran the whole e2e suite, not just the conversation file.\n- `yarn check:conventions` and `yarn format:check`: both pass.\n- I did not run the new cancellation assertion against the unfixed code, so I have not seen it fail before the fix.\n\n**Unclear points, decided by me:**\n- The traveller's report says \"email hidden on their side too\". The fix covers that: the same paid-stay check governs emails and phone numbers.\n- I did not start a server, so port 4471 was not used.\n- The `jest` invocation without `yarn test:e2e` fails on ESM loading, which is a local setup issue unrelated to this change.",
